# Normalise line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows; Render and Vercel build on Linux. Without
# this, every file committed from Windows shows as fully rewritten in a diff
# made on another platform, and code review becomes unusable.
#
# Text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they fail to execute on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Batch and PowerShell files are Windows-only and want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated. Collapse in pull requests so reviews show real changes.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
